.DS_Store
node_modules

# Production-generated content. These files are written on the server by the
# admin dashboard (post images, gallery images, notices, CV uploads). Tracking
# them made every deployment re-assert a frozen snapshot of this directory over
# the live one, which is why admin-uploaded media disappeared after each push.
# Code belongs in git; uploaded content belongs on the server only.
# uploads/.htaccess stays tracked because it is security config, not content.
uploads/*
!uploads/.htaccess

# Persistent upload storage. Created at runtime by storage.php and never
# committed: a path the repository does not contain is not touched by the
# Hostinger deployment, which is exactly the property uploads/ lacked.
media/

# Private database credentials. Lives ONLY on the server (create it via the
# Hostinger File Manager from db.config.example.php); never committed, so the
# real password never enters this public repository.
backend/Database/db.config.php

# Local-only diagnostic. Never commit: when executed on a live server it prints
# the database host/user/name, the password length, the full table list and
# every admin email + role — with no authentication. Keeping it out of the
# repository is what keeps it off the deployed site.
db_check.php
